Shorter superpermutations

The superpermutations in words/ re-join the component words of the superpermutations on 11, 12 and 13 symbols
(43,930,680, 522,745,581 and 6,747,918,066 letters) from https://github.com/jaypantone/superperm-upper-43-80 (Apache License 2.0),
by Jay Pantone. The construction of those components is entirely Pantone's; this repository only changes where each
component is opened and in what order the components are joined.

The gap-2 opening used for the n=11 and n=12 words was identified in rumstd's n=10 superpermutation of length 4,034,873
(pull request #3 to jaypantone/superperm-upper-43-80). The 43,930,644 word was found starting from rumstd's
43,930,668 word (pull request #4), which builds on Theo H.'s 43,930,678 word (pull request #2).

By Jakub Halfar, with Claude (Opus 5.5) in Claude Code. Jakub Halfar chose the problem and directed the work; Claude
